&lt;div class="word-content">
&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:-.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:
18.0pt'>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>              We do not need to decide
between the “theories of inspiration” to understand how scripture came to have
the character of “God-breathedness” (2 Timothy &lt;b>3&lt;/b>:16). As we can judge
from scripture itself, God operated in more than one way in producing scripture.
The models of origin may be organized according to what God specially gave to
his human spokesmen.  &lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>PASSAGES RELEVANT TO INERRANCY</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/revelation-scripture-bibliology/scripture/passages-relevant-to-inerrancy/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/revelation-scripture-bibliology/scripture/passages-relevant-to-inerrancy/</guid><description>&lt;style>
